Why Is Demand Increasing
• Wind energy expansion — Fiberglass-reinforced composites are widely used in wind turbine blades because of their strength-to-weight ratio and corrosion resistance.

• Construction and infrastructure growth — Fiberglass is used in reinforcement, panels, pipes and tanks because of its durability, lightweight characteristics and corrosion resistance.

• Automotive lightweighting — Fiberglass composites are increasingly used in automotive body panels, interior components and structural parts as manufacturers pursue lower weight and improved efficiency.

Materials & Composite Technology Watch: Fiberglass Expands Across Energy and Electronics
Fiberglass demand is increasingly connected to composite-material development. Wind energy remains an important application because longer turbine blades require materials combining strength, low weight and durability. Construction also continues to use fiberglass for insulation and reinforcement applications.

Another opportunity is emerging from electronics and telecommunications. Fiberglass provides electrical insulation and dimensional stability for printed circuit board substrates, supporting demand associated with high-frequency applications and network expansion. Manufacturers are also exploring advanced products with improved strength, fire resistance and sustainability profiles, including hybrid composites and bio-based resin systems.

