Why This Market Matters
Fiberglass is increasingly important across industries seeking lightweight, durable and corrosion-resistant materials. Its role in wind turbine blades connects the market directly with renewable-energy infrastructure, while construction and transportation applications provide additional demand.

The industry also faces challenges. Volatility in raw material and energy costs can affect manufacturing economics, while environmental and health regulations require additional compliance measures. Recycling fiberglass composites remains difficult, creating pressure for more sustainable end-of-life solutions.

